1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,645
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:04,645 --> 00:00:10,164
Ellen, I'd like your opinion.

3
00:00:10,164 --> 00:00:11,394
About what?

4
00:00:11,394 --> 00:00:15,730
Well, Richard and I feel that with a baby coming

5
00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:21,664
we need to have our own place to live.

6
00:00:21,664 --> 00:00:21,937
Oh.

7
00:00:21,937 --> 00:00:24,286
Well, what do you think about Richard and me

8
00:00:24,286 --> 00:00:26,132
looking for a small house or an apartment

9
00:00:26,132 --> 00:00:30,109
at this point in our lives?

10
00:00:30,109 --> 00:00:31,753
We love having you here,

11
00:00:31,753 --> 00:00:33,326
and there is room,

12
00:00:33,326 --> 00:00:36,200
and ... and when the baby comes,

13
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:39,381
the baby can stay in your room for a while.

14
00:00:39,381 --> 00:00:47,937
Richard feels we need to find a small house.

15
00:00:47,937 --> 00:00:51,000
I remember when I was pregnant with Richard.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,252
Philip and I were living with Grandma and Grandpa.

17
00:00:54,252 --> 00:00:55,874
Philip was a young doctor,

18
00:00:55,874 --> 00:01:00,899
and he kept talking about having a house of our own.

19
00:01:00,899 --> 00:01:02,309
It's natural.

20
00:01:02,309 --> 00:01:03,137
What did you do?

21
00:01:03,137 --> 00:01:07,835
We looked at a lot of houses.

22
00:01:07,835 --> 00:01:08,493
Did you find one?

23
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:09,937
Oh, not at first.

24
00:01:09,937 --> 00:01:11,471
We couldn't afford it.

25
00:01:11,471 --> 00:01:16,449
Grandpa wanted to lend us the money to buy one,

26
00:01:16,449 --> 00:01:18,503
but Philip is too independent.

27
00:01:18,503 --> 00:01:21,065
He didn't want to borrow any money.

28
00:01:21,065 --> 00:01:23,883
Sounds like Richard.

29
00:01:23,883 --> 00:01:25,383
They're all alike.

30
00:01:25,383 --> 00:01:27,111
Richard is a real Stewart.

31
00:01:27,111 --> 00:01:29,839
He's independent,

32
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:32,984
and sometimes just stubborn.

33
00:01:32,984 --> 00:01:37,082
When did you buy a house?

34
00:01:37,082 --> 00:01:39,273
After Richard was born.

35
00:01:39,273 --> 00:01:43,171
I was teaching music,

36
00:01:43,171 --> 00:01:46,079
and Philip was opening his first medical office.

37
00:01:46,079 --> 00:01:47,707
Where was the house?

38
00:01:47,707 --> 00:01:49,707
Right here in Riverdale.

39
00:01:49,707 --> 00:01:52,105
Of course, it was a small house,

40
00:01:52,105 --> 00:01:54,139
but just right for us.

41
00:01:54,139 --> 00:01:58,113
It's funny. History repeats itself.

42
00:01:58,113 --> 00:02:02,659
Now Richard and I are having a baby,

43
00:02:02,659 --> 00:02:03,971
and we probably won't be able to

44
00:02:03,971 --> 00:02:05,074
afford a house right away, either.

45
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:09,332
Why don't you look at some houses, Marilyn?

46
00:02:09,332 --> 00:02:14,008
Good idea. \u597D\u4E3B\u610F\u3002

47
00:02:14,008 --> 00:02:16,986
Look in the real-estate section of Sunday's Times.

48
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:18,986
You'll learn a lot.

49
00:02:18,986 --> 00:02:19,736
Maybe we should

50
00:02:19,736 --> 00:02:22,942
speak to a real-estate agent about a house.

51
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,920
And a bank about a mortgage.

52
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:28,898
I'll talk to Richard about it.

53
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:30,388
I think it's a good idea, Ellen.

54
00:02:30,388 --> 00:02:31,876
We can learn a lot by asking.

55
00:02:31,876 --> 00:02:34,854
And if I can be of any help,

56
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:36,047
let me know.

57
00:02:36,047 --> 00:02:37,832
As a matter of fact,

58
00:02:37,832 --> 00:02:40,810
my friend Virginia Martinelli is a real-estate agent.

59
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:41,239
Good.

60
00:02:41,239 --> 00:02:42,953
You won't believe this,

61
00:02:42,953 --> 00:02:47,099
but she sold us our first house and this one.

62
00:02:47,099 --> 00:02:48,433
Well, I'll tell Richard,

63
00:02:48,433 --> 00:02:55,700
and we'll go to see her.

64
00:02:55,700 --> 00:03:01,656
Do you think the skirt length is right, Ellen?

65
00:03:01,656 --> 00:03:04,634
Do you think it's too long?

66
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:07,612
I think the skirt is just right.

67
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:10,589
Are you planning to attach a train to it?

68
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:13,567
No. No train. Just the dress.

69
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:17,955
But I am going to make a headpiece of lace.

70
00:03:17,955 --> 00:03:21,803
That dress is gorgeous.

71
00:03:21,803 --> 00:03:22,501
Thanks, Ellen.

72
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:25,479
And thanks for the advice about the house.

73
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:27,452
I'll talk to Richard about it

74
00:03:27,452 --> 00:03:29,657
the minute he comes home.

75
00:03:29,657 --> 00:03:31,435
And remember,

76
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:34,413
we love having you here.

77
00:03:34,413 --> 00:03:37,413
There's no need to rush.
